the raiders picking up their first  preseason win of the season this past  saturday in front of fans at allegiant  stadium 8 sports now kevin martin  joining us with a recap of the win  reaction from fans who were in  attendance for the very first time it  was certainly a big deal kevin yeah you  know preseason wins don't typically hold  much meaning but saturday's 20-7 victory  over seattle wasn't your typical  preseason game it was the first raiders  game at allegiant stadium with fans in  attendance more than 50 thousand fans  were on hand saturday to witness history  as third string quarterback nathan  peterman led the offense going 29-39 for  246 yards and an interception while the  silver max defense held seattle just one  touchdown and while it was clear raider  nation was happy to be back in allegiant  stadium cheering on their squad the team  was just as thrilled to have their fans  in the building  it was great to have the raider fans out  there by the way  kind of numb you know just uh to see the  world coming back together  and to be in this stadium with these  fans again it um  it just warms my heart i thank them all  for coming out and um  you know we we are really really excited  about playing in front of them for the  rest of this year  the raiders now have two more preseason  games both on the road and then they'll  return home for their first regular  season home opener against baltimore on  monday night football on september 13th  kiersten
 

